530	     * Reports whether a response naming the given city should carry a capacity warning. The warning is
531	     * active once the city already holds between {@link #CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD} and one fewer
532	     * than {@link #MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY} owners (40-49), signalling that it is approaching the per-city
533	     * capacity limit. Owners are grouped into a city case-insensitively after surrounding whitespace is
534	     * trimmed and internal runs are collapsed, mirroring {@link #rejectCityAtCapacity}. The hard
535	     * rejection at {@link #MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY} is unaffected.
536	     *
537	     * @param city the city to evaluate
538	     * @return {@code true} when the city holds between the warning threshold and the capacity limit
539	     *         (exclusive) owners, otherwise {@code false}
540	     */
541	    private boolean isCapacityWarningActive(String city) {
542	        String normalizedCity = normalizeHouseholdField(city);
543	        long ownersInCity = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
544	            .filter(existing -> normalizeHouseholdField(existing.getCity()).equals(normalizedCity))
545	            .count();
546	        return ownersInCity >= CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD && ownersInCity < MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY;
